@flexiarg operator/defer-with-a-named-trigger
@title defer with a named trigger
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 4 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade; THEN worded 4 ways across its proposals
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-6paVBT turn-Hef9Yp turn-LPlWIF turn-kv3qZ7; first proposed for: A choice is accepted for now.
@why [musn/declare-scope]

! conclusion: Defer explicitly, name what would reopen the question, and record what stands meanwhile.

  + IF:
    He says if we want to revisit it later, we can revisit it later.

  + HOWEVER:
    The reopening condition is left open ('if we want').

  + THEN:
    Defer explicitly, name what would reopen the question, and record what stands meanwhile.

  + BECAUSE:
    A provisional choice should be reopenable.
